        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg-loop" value="Loop repo" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=9;fontStyle=1;strokeWidth=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="580" y="380" width="80" height="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg-e-self" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;fontSize=10;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#00897b;" edge="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="510" y="432" as="sourcePoint" /><mxPoint x="550" y="432" as="targetPoint" /></mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="leg-t-self" value="loop fixes itself" style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="560" y="420" width="110" height="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="example" value="&lt;b style=&quot;margin-right:0.25em&quot;&gt;The loop fixes itself.&lt;/b&gt;An agent that hits a problem in the loop (a skill, the reviewer, CI) reports it to the orchestrator. The fix ships as a PR to the loop's own repo. Workflow fixes reach every repo when the v0 tag moves; skill fixes ship as a plugin update. Nazar's only steps: approve and merge.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;margin-right:0.25em&quot;&gt;Example:&lt;/b&gt;factory-loop #16 and #14, review-job fixes raised by an agent from forge-cli PRs: a false red review check, and review runs that stopped early. Both were merged and rolled out via v0; after #14, the next review on forge-cli #42 passed." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=8;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="20" y="550" width="710" height="105" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
